WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:03.055
Design the tables for a ride-hailing app.

2
00:00:03.075 --> 00:00:04.805
This is the modeling round.

3
00:00:04.825 --> 00:00:07.915
The first five minutes decide the rest of the hour.

4
00:00:07.935 --> 00:00:12.990
Three ideas carry you: the grain, facts and dimensions, and history.

5
00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:14.675
First: the grain.

6
00:00:14.695 --> 00:00:16.475
The grain says what one row means.

7
00:00:16.495 --> 00:00:18.985
For example: one row per trip.

8
00:00:19.005 --> 00:00:21.135
Say it out loud before you draw anything.

9
00:00:21.155 --> 00:00:23.745
It decides the keys and the measures.

10
00:00:23.765 --> 00:00:28.195
Mix two grains in one table, and your sums count things twice.

11
00:00:28.215 --> 00:00:30.480
Second: facts and dimensions.

12
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.868
A fact is something that happened, with numbers.

13
00:00:32.888 --> 00:00:35.590
A trip, with a fare and a distance.

14
00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.415
A dimension is the context.

15
00:00:37.435 --> 00:00:40.275
The driver, the rider, the city, the date.

16
00:00:40.295 --> 00:00:42.463
Facts in the middle, dimensions around them.

17
00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:45.275
That shape is the star schema.

18
00:00:45.295 --> 00:00:48.185
Third: what happens when a dimension changes?

19
00:00:48.205 --> 00:00:50.397
A driver moves from Pune to Mumbai.

20
00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.795
Old trips must still show Pune.

21
00:00:52.815 --> 00:00:54.232
So do not overwrite.

22
00:00:54.252 --> 00:00:58.170
Close the old row with an end date, and add a new row.

23
00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.680
Last: how wide should the table be?

24
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.665
In a columnar warehouse, joins cost more than extra columns.

25
00:01:04.685 --> 00:01:07.390
So a wide table is often fine for serving.

26
00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:10.440
Keep the star as the source of truth.

27
00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.750
Quick recap of data modeling.

28
00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:14.062
Say the grain first.

29
00:01:14.082 --> 00:01:15.875
Facts with dimensions around them.

30
00:01:15.895 --> 00:01:18.135
And type 2 keeps history.

31
00:01:18.155 --> 00:01:21.255
Now start the first lesson below.
